From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] Default-initialize Print + WipeTower POD members

OrcaSlicer's Print and WipeTower classes carry POD members
(numeric/struct fields without ctors) that are left uninitialized in
the headers. On Debug Linux desktop builds the stack happens to land
on zero so the bug is dormant, but Release Android arm64 builds with
a different stack layout read garbage on first access. Symptoms
observed in the wild include nonsense wipe-tower coordinates,
m_isBBLPrinter flipping arbitrarily true (which then drives our
nativeSlice into the BBL config-dump path and crashes inside
ConfigOptionEnumsGeneric — see patch 0011), and stale plate origins.

Patch 0011 already neutralizes the m_isBBLPrinter symptom from JNI
by force-setting `print.is_BBL_printer() = false` in slic3r_jni.cpp.
That fix only covers the BBL flag for the slice we drive ourselves;
this patch fixes all the other dormant fields at the source so any
future code path is safe (multi-color slicing exercises FakeWipeTower
heavily, for example).

Catalog of fields initialized:

  src/libslic3r/Print.hpp::FakeWipeTower
    pos, width, height, layer_height, depth, brim_width,
    rotation_angle, cone_angle, plate_origin
    (the std::vector / std::map members already self-initialize,
     and rib_offset already had {0.f,0.f}.)

  src/libslic3r/Print.hpp::Print
    m_isBBLPrinter (now redundant with patch 0011's runtime guard
                    but cheap defense-in-depth)
    m_origin

  src/libslic3r/GCode/WipeTower.hpp::WipeTower
    m_cur_layer_id

Independently confirmed in taylormadearmy/u1-slicer-for-android's
ENGINE_UPGRADE_GUIDE.md (AGPL — same license family as libslic3r),
where they hit exactly this class of bug on Android NDK release
builds and traced it to the same fields. They report 436 vs 840
tool changes on a multi-color H2C Benchy as one symptom.

To retire: when upstream OrcaSlicer (or the Snapmaker fork) lands
the same default-initializers, delete this file.

diff --git a/src/libslic3r/GCode/WipeTower.hpp b/src/libslic3r/GCode/WipeTower.hpp
index e03c543903..17125a7cad 100644
--- a/src/libslic3r/GCode/WipeTower.hpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/GCode/WipeTower.hpp
@@ -437,7 +437,7 @@ private:
     size_t m_first_layer_idx    = size_t(-1);
 
     std::vector<double> m_filaments_change_length;
-    size_t       m_cur_layer_id;
+    size_t       m_cur_layer_id = 0;
     NozzleChangeResult m_nozzle_change_result;
     std::vector<int>   m_filament_map;
     bool               m_has_tpu_filament{false};
diff --git a/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp b/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
index b98811c8e3..99b33a00b7 100644
--- a/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
+++ b/src/libslic3r/Print.hpp
@@ -591,16 +591,16 @@ private:
 struct FakeWipeTower
 {
     // generate fake extrusion
-    Vec2f pos;
-    float width;
-    float height;
-    float layer_height;// Due to variable layer height, this parameter may be not right.
-    float depth;
+    Vec2f pos{0.f, 0.f};
+    float width{0.f};
+    float height{0.f};
+    float layer_height{0.f};// Due to variable layer height, this parameter may be not right.
+    float depth{0.f};
     std::vector<std::pair<float, float>> z_and_depth_pairs;
-    float brim_width;
-    float rotation_angle;
-    float cone_angle;
-    Vec2d plate_origin;
+    float brim_width{0.f};
+    float rotation_angle{0.f};
+    float cone_angle{0.f};
